{"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:21TelemetryDeckEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder.swift#L85","fileName":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder.swift"},"title":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/init(appID:testMode:plan:limit:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"anchor":"Type-Aliases","title":"Type Aliases","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and its limits:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let telemetryDeck = try HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(","    appID: appID,  \/\/ from the app's settings in the TelemetryDeck dashboard","    namespace: \"com.example\",  \/\/ your organization's namespace","    testMode: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose signals only Test Mode should show","    plan: plan)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON array of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one event per record, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first. Each event is a flat object of these members:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The app ID the encoder is made with, without leading or trailing whitespace"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientUser"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SHA256 of the record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":" as a lowercase UUID string, as 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits; of the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" the same way when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isTestMode"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"\"true\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"false\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the encoder is made with","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"receivedAt","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601, in UTC with milliseconds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; left out when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.SDK.name"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each of the event’s stored properties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its value, read through the event’s schema in the plan; a nested value spread into one member per scalar it holds, named after its path, joined by "},{"code":".","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"cart.size","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"tags.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent, hashed as TelemetryDeck’s SDKs hash a user’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier with their default, empty salt; TelemetryDeck salts and hashes it again before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storing it. No salt of the app’s own is taken: ","type":"text"},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends the same session in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clear, so a salt would hide nothing. TelemetryDeck counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so its users","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are sessions. A record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or one a store recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is its own user of one event, with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"sessionID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", linked to nothing: TelemetryDeck","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refuses an event without a ","type":"text"},{"code":"clientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any other context value, aren’t sent. Nor is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"floatValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": a number among the properties","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its JSON type in Ingest API v3.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, and so is an element of an array. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out too, as TelemetryDeck stores no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value for it. TelemetryDeck stores a nested object without indexing it and leaves arrays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"undefined, so the encoder spreads both into members of their own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event also holds these of TelemetryDeck’s built-in parameters, for each of the keys the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s context has a value for:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.AppInfo.version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"TelemetryDeck.AppInfo.buildNumber","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The version and the build, each left out when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.AppInfo.versionAndBuildNumber"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with both a version and a build","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2.4.1 (build 418)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.modelName","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The model","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.operatingSystem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.platform","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The operating system’s name, ","type":"text"},{"code":"iOS","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.systemVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.systemMajorVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.Device.systemMajorMinorVersion"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"},{"type":"text","text":", with a version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The name and the version, its first component and its first two: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iOS 26.1.0"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iOS 26"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iOS 26.1"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.RunContext.locale","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The locale’s identifier, ","type":"text"},{"code":"en_US","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeck.RunContext.language"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with a language"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The language’s code, ","type":"text"},{"code":"en","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"TelemetryDeck.UserPreference.region","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"},{"text":", with a region","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region’s code, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"US"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name or parameter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name TelemetryDeck refuses or keeps for itself, one whose values flatten to one name, one whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is outside the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"years 1 to 9999, and one whose JSON is over 333,333 bytes ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. TelemetryDeck answers a request it takes with 200, and checks every event of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request before storing any: it answers 422 when one breaks a rule, which "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops and reports with every record of the request. It answers 503 when its queue is full,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" retries. It doesn’t remove duplicates, so a record sent again is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counted again. The bytes are the same for the same records on every run and platform: no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of TelemetryDeck’s Ingest API v3, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to an organization’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/v3\/<namespace>\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckbatchencoder"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/H